  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Concentrated nitric acid is a strong oxidising agent and attacks most metals except noble metals such as gold and platinum. The&nbsp;products of oxidation depend upon the concentration of the acid, temperature and the nature of the material undergoing oxidation.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PbS</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>dil</mi><mo>.</mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Pb</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>NO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi></math> is paramagnetic due to the presence of unpaired electron. It is a neutral oxide. It is colourless.</p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;are correct statements.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
